                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "af7ae0a9-ef36-42b7-873c-80ec7730f3d7",
                                "sense_id": "c90dc7c3-a7ea-32af-98f5-baab07f43248",
                                "text": "Selbstverständlich macht er sich auch keine Hoffnungen, das Prozess zu gewinnen; er hätte die Klage angeblich eingereicht, weil Lipstadt ihn als Holokaustleugner verleumdet hat; anstatt sich einen Verteidiger zu holen und diese \"Verleumdung\" Lipstadts zu dementieren, erzählt er vor einem möglichst breiten Publikum, *warum* er ein Holokaustleugner ist.",
                                "translation": "He has, of course, no hope of winning the trial himself; he professedly filed the suit because Lipstadt slandered him as a Holocaust denier; instead of hiring a defence lawyer and denying this \"slander\" by Lipstadt, he is recounting to the broadest possible audience *why* he is a Holocaust denier.",
                                "english": "He has, of course, no hope of winning the trial himself; he professedly filed the suit because Lipstadt slandered him as a Holocaust denier; instead of hiring a defence lawyer and denying this \"slander\" by Lipstadt, he is recounting to the broadest possible audience *why* he is a Holocaust denier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ecfd0d4-c2c2-43bc-a446-a21d19eedb9d",
                                "sense_id": "c90dc7c3-a7ea-32af-98f5-baab07f43248",
                                "text": "Das Mahnmal mit der Existenz der Holokaustleugner zu begründen, tut den Leugnern zu viel der Ehre an und bringt die Mahnmalidee selbst in ein schiefes Licht.",
                                "translation": "To justify the memorial on the basis of the existence of Holocaust deniers does the deniers too much credit and distorts the idea of the memorial itself.",
                                "english": "To justify the memorial on the basis of the existence of Holocaust deniers does the deniers too much credit and distorts the idea of the memorial itself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57627a77-11ca-4149-8f7c-0d01acf8d867",
                                "sense_id": "c90dc7c3-a7ea-32af-98f5-baab07f43248",
                                "text": "Das Delikt brauch hier weder ausgeführt noch versucht worden zu sein ([…] BGE 127 IV 203, 207 f. – Holokaustleugner; […]).",
                                "translation": "The offence does not need to have been committed or attempted here ( […] BGE 127 IV 203, 207 f. – Holocaust deniers; […] ).",
                                "english": "The offence does not need to have been committed or attempted here ( […] BGE 127 IV 203, 207 f. – Holocaust deniers; […] )."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
